4 active nodes) and the presence of hubs like 800/933 are confounders, but hub co-membership does not yield a directed, delay-bounded chain."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion**\n\nKey findings:\n- 695 has only **5 events / 5 partners** and 1495 only **4 events / 4 partners** in the window (step_02) \u2014 this is a sparse, not a hub-driven, situation.\n- 695's neighbourhood {663, 800, 886, 918, 1468} and 1495's {362, 701, 702, 1517} are **disjoint** (steps 04, 05), and the 2-hop expansions of the two nodes (steps 03, 06) share no node that would bridge them in the required direction.\n- Direction matters: 695's **only out-edge** in the entire window is 695\u21921468 (step_15), and 1495's **only in-edge** is 1517\u21921495 (step_16). 1468's out-neighbours (step_03) do not include 1517 or any of 1517's in-neighbours {1301, 1474, 1514} (step_06). So no directed chain 695\u2192\u2026\u21921495 exists even when time is ignored.\n- Timing also fails: 695's activity clusters at ~30.4k, ~58.7k, ~59.3k, ~63k, ~64k (steps 07, 09, 11) while 1495's in-contact from 1517 falls in [60125, 61624] (steps 12, 14). 695 emits nothing in [58625, 59524] out-bound (step_13), and the gaps between the 695-side and 1495-side events far exceed the 600-unit relay limit.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.88,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 695 to 1495 exists under a 600-unit relay limit. The failure is structural as well as temporal: 695's sole outgoing contact in the window is to 1468, and 1495's sole incoming contact is from 1517, but 1468's out-neighbourhood and 1517's in-neighbourhood are disjoint and 2-hop expansions of the two nodes share no bridging node. Temporally, 695's events (~30.4k, 58.7k, 59.3k, 63k, 64k) and the 1517->1495 contact in [60125, 61624] are separated by gaps far larger than 600 units, with no intervening relay chain. High graph-wide volume (7526 events, 1954 active nodes) and the presence of hubs like 800/933 are confounders, but hub co-membership does not yield a directed, delay-bounded chain.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 61731, "total_output_tokens": 9141, "total_tokens": 70872, "total_latency_ms": 132891, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}